Q: How to copy files from an absolute path to docker image using docker maven plugin A: <p>Include the shared/common resources in your pom  by adding:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;resources&gt;
    &lt;resource&gt;
        &lt;directory&gt;/absolute/path/to/resources&lt;/directory&gt;
        &lt;includes&gt;
            &lt;include&gt;**/*&lt;/include&gt;
        &lt;/includes&gt;
        &lt;targetPath&gt;shared&lt;/targetPath&gt;
    &lt;/resource&gt;
&lt;/resources&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>Then (if using spotify Dockerfile maven plugin) add the resource path on build as a build argument</p>

<pre><code>&lt;configuration&gt;
    ...
    &lt;buildArgs&gt;
        ...
        &lt;SHARED_RESOURCES&gt;target/classes/shared&lt;/SHARED_RESOURCES&gt;
    &lt;/buildArgs&gt;
&lt;/configuration&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>Then use it in Dockerfile as such:</p>

<pre><code>...
ARG SHARED_RESOURCES
COPY ${SHARED_RESOURCES}/something /target
...
</code></pre>

